#: apps/logica/web/logica.js:930
Los analizadores "24 MHz 8 canales" (clones del Saleae Logic, con un Cypress FX2LP) no tienen programa propio: la app les carga fx2lafw, el firmware libre de sigrok, cada vez que se enchufan. Bajá "sigrok-firmware-fx2lafw" (el .tar.gz de binarios) y subilo acá tal cual: la página saca los .fw y los pone en la carpeta logica/fx2lafw.	The "24 MHz 8 channel" analysers (Saleae Logic clones, with a Cypress FX2LP) have no program of their own: the app loads fx2lafw, sigrok's open firmware, every time they are plugged in. Download "sigrok-firmware-fx2lafw" (the binaries' .tar.gz) and upload it here as it is: the page takes the .fw files out and puts them in the logica/fx2lafw folder.

